# SwiftFormat configuration for Hyper Meta AI.
#
# This config describes the style the codebase already uses, so that running
# `swiftformat .` on a clean checkout is close to a no-op. A formatter that
# produces a 20,000-line diff on first run gets turned off instead of adopted,
# so anything that would mass-rewrite existing code is disabled below with a
# note on what it would take to turn on.
#
# Options are deliberately few. Every one listed here was checked against
# SwiftFormat's own option definitions; unset options keep their defaults rather
# than being spelled out speculatively.

--swiftversion 5.10
--exclude build,DerivedData,.build,HyperMetaAI/Generated

# 196 of 276 files indent with 4 spaces, 80 with 2. Unifying is mechanical but
# touches nearly every file, so `indent` stays off until that is done as its own
# commit. Enabling it here would mix reformatting into every future diff.
--disable indent

# Matches the existing wrapping style: 88 lines exceed 120 characters today,
# mostly long Chinese comments and DAT SDK call chains.
--maxwidth 140
--wraparguments before-first
--wrapparameters before-first
--wrapcollections before-first
--closingparen balanced
--funcattributes prev-line
--typeattributes prev-line

--self remove
--semicolons never

# 1,200 multi-line lists end without a trailing comma against 53 that have one.
# SwiftFormat defaults to `always`, which would rewrite all 1,200, so pin it to
# match the code. This also keeps it consistent with SwiftLint's trailing_comma.
--trailingcommas never
--importgrouping testable-last
--trimwhitespace always
--stripunusedargs closure-only
--header ignore
--elseposition same-line
--guardelse auto
--shortoptionals always

# `// MARK:` sections organise the large view files; do not reflow them.
--disable blankLinesAroundMark

# The audio pipeline uses explicit `return` in short closures where it clarifies
# which branch produces the value.
--disable redundantReturn

# Collapsing if/else chains into a single assignment obscures the realtime state
# transitions in the voice path, where each branch is read on its own.
--disable conditionalAssignment

--enable isEmpty
--enable blockComments
--enable redundantOptionalBinding
--enable sortImports
--enable wrapMultilineStatementBraces
